  "id": "Compound::DB00799 - Gene::6257",
  "verbalization": "Tazarotene, a retinoid, is consistently linked to Rxrb through a series of molecular pathways that involve retinoid metabolism and binding. The evidence suggests that Tazarotene, as part of the retinoid family, binds to Rxrb through a shared mechanism involving retinoic acid agents and carbonyl compounds. This is supported by multiple paths that indicate Tazarotene's inclusion in retinoids, which in turn bind to Rxrb, suggesting a conserved interaction across different retinoid compounds. The lowest common ancestors across these paths point to retinoic acid agents and carbonyl compounds, reinforcing the biochemical link between Tazarotene and Rxrb. The presence of multiple retinoid compounds (Bexarotene, Adapalene, Acitretin) all binding to Rxrb further supports the hypothesis that the interaction is not specific to a single retinoid but is a broader molecular property of retinoids. The integrated evidence suggests that Tazarotene exerts its effect through a mechanism involving retinoic acid metabolism and binding to Rxrb, with the observed scores reflecting the strength of this relationship in the dataset.",
